! conclusion: Keep Joe-facing working surfaces in futon0 and consolidate outward-facing work in futon7 as the stack's cyborg/Markov-blanket architectural axis.

  + context: War Room decision WR-17 (2026-05-17). Operator: Joe. The axis under which M-interim-director operates and the self-sustaining pilot will run.

  + IF:
    Work can be distinguished by whether it faces Joe's working surface or the stack's outward environment.

  + THEN:
    Place Joe-working-surface work in futon0 and outward-facing work in futon7; after the pilot, evaluate whether the cut should become a substrate shape in S9's frame.

  + BECAUSE:
    The cut is consistent with the AIF² Markov-blanket framing used by the self-sustaining pilot.

    + evidence: Bulletin 9 names futon0 as the Joe-facing cyborg layer, futon7 as the outward-facing Markov blanket, and M-interim-director as operating under this architectural axis.
